{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"y":0.031976744435390891,"h":0.014548579711374798,"t":"Test 1","x":0.092592593440931056,"w":0.059670778910319008,"c":1},{"w":0.018518517812093099,"t":"G","h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.092592592842924634,"y":0.48255813932389147},{"x":0.12551441444406786,"h":0.019140164899882128,"w":0.75925923665364581,"y":0.079799764503204917,"t":"The burial chamber of the tomb, where the king's body was laid to rest, was dug","c":1},{"h":0.017476100382451065,"c":1,"w":0.74485595703125007,"x":0.13786008702298563,"t":"beneath the base of the pyramid, surrounded by a vast maze of long tunnels that","y":0.098837209135327342},{"c":1,"t":"had rooms off them to discourage robbers. One of the most mysterious discoveries","w":0.767489725748698,"y":0.11773255797925142,"x":0.13786007528977498,"h":0.017441860778592999},{"y":0.13662790678982928,"t":"found inside the pyramid was a large number of stone vessels. Over 40,000 of","x":0.13786008098840655,"w":0.73045267740885433,"h":0.020348837575025036,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.75514404296874993,"x":0.13786007717616486,"y":0.15694935200679827,"t":"these vessels, of various forms and shapes, were discovered in storerooms off the","h":0.017469252798666735},{"w":0.77160491943359366,"y":0.17579505305313692,"h":0.01751890058933081,"t":"pyramid's underground passages. They are inscribed with the names of rulers from","x":0.13786009162408097,"c":1},{"y":0.1946407540994084,"t":"the First and Second Dynasties of Egypt and made from different kinds of stone.","w":0.75514404296874993,"h":0.017667844522968101,"c":1,"x":0.13580246399912965},{"x":0.13786009095966581,"w":0.72016459147135425,"y":0.21366279053699,"t":"There is no agreement among scholars and archaeologists on why the vessels","h":0.017491508569256853,"c":1},{"w":0.74485595703125007,"t":"were placed in the tomb of Djoser or what they were supposed to represent. The","h":0.018895349176808907,"x":0.13786008094939575,"c":1,"y":0.23110465131844471},{"x":0.1377919865118318,"y":0.25117910930840548,"t":"archaeologist Jean-Philippe Lauer, who excavated most of the pyramid and complex,","w":0.79437759399414076,"c":1,"h":0.020353816002080749},{"c":1,"x":0.13786007268325326,"t":"believes they were originally stored and then given aiproper burial' by Djoser in his","y":0.27031802120054316,"w":0.78600824991861973,"h":0.018926164427129244},{"t":"pyramid to honor his predecessors. There are other historians, however, who claim","w":0.76762379964192706,"h":0.021338731296211333,"x":0.13780037961669336,"y":0.28876505578052836,"c":1},{"y":0.30948174310805276,"c":1,"t":"the vessels were dumped into the shafts as yet another attempt to prevent grave","w":0.73662551879882809,"h":0.017667844522968323,"x":0.13786007988356005},{"x":0.13786007874600334,"t":"robbers from getting to the king's burial chamber.","w":0.46707819620768221,"h":0.017667844522968101,"c":1,"y":0.3297997645159163},{"w":0.79218109130859371,"y":0.35747938766917264,"c":1,"h":0.017520612485276699,"x":0.13991768469495733,"t":"Unfortunately, all of the precautions and intricate design of the underground network"},{"w":0.74910247802734375,"h":0.021587753745214933,"c":1,"x":0.13779341691018998,"y":0.37387539341660991,"t":"did not prevent ancient robbers from finding a way in. Djoser's grave goods, and"},{"h":0.01896211648857915,"w":0.74691360473632806,"x":0.13786006995272526,"y":0.39534883759792372,"c":1,"t":"even his body, were stolen at some point in the past and all archaeologists found"},{"y":0.41357166835130443,"x":0.13984422068963351,"t":"were a small number of his valuables overlooked by the thieves. There was enough","w":0.76969334920247379,"h":0.020399978781476591,"c":1},{"y":0.43240066552880885,"c":1,"w":0.75326044718424479,"h":0.022107496138034644,"t":"left throughout the pyramid and its complex, however, to astonish and amaze the","x":0.1357146126847357},{"x":0.13786008235949404,"w":0.30452674865722656,"t":"archaeologists who excavated it.","h":0.017455556507806946,"c":1,"y":0.45347467619974235},{"t":"Egyptologist Miroslav Verner writes, 'Few monuments hold a place in human","x":0.13786008187942345,"h":0.017441860778592888,"y":0.48255813937545389,"w":0.72427983601888024,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"history as significant as that of the Step Pyramid in Saqgara... It can be said","x":0.13580247782429022,"w":0.72016459147135425,"y":0.50145348821284141,"h":0.017441860778592999},{"h":0.017472676590558955,"c":1,"y":0.52031802123708148,"x":0.13786009007446354,"t":"without exaggeration that this pyramid complex constitutes a milestone in the","w":0.72633743286132812},{"c":1,"h":0.019140164899882239,"x":0.13786007541212322,"w":0.767489725748698,"y":0.5376914013561841,"t":"evolution of monumental stone architecture in Egypt and in the world as a whole.?'"},{"t":"The Step Pyramid was a revolutionary advance in architecture and became the","x":0.13786008912094189,"y":0.55800942276071719,"w":0.73251027425130211,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"t":"archetype which all the other great pyramid builders of Egypt would follow.","x":0.13786008376982625,"h":0.017506916756062751,"y":0.57848837193348068,"w":0.71193415323893228,"c":1},{"y":0.90552325563693892,"t":"22","w":0.024691357612609863,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.092592592705105475,"c":1}]}